&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You and the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline’s mission is to create the first logistics system that serves all humans equally. As an Operations Program Manager, you’ll lead cross-functional programs that make our delivery network safer, more reliable, and more efficient as it grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own selected programs from defining the problem through rollout, adoption, and measuring results. Your work may include preparing operations for new capabilities, improving maintenance and service workflows, introducing new hardware, and supporting multiple delivery models on shared infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll spend time at operating sites alongside field teams and work with Operations leaders, Engineering, and other teams to turn what you learn into improvements the network can use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead day-to-day execution.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead daily and weekly work across teams. Keep the critical path clear, resolve blockers and handoff gaps, and make decisions within your scope. Bring recommendations to leadership when tradeoffs need their input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure what changes.&lt;/strong&gt; Set baselines and success measures. Work with operators and technical teams to find the causes of performance gaps and check whether fixes improve safety, reliability, cost, capacity, productivity, or customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve how teams work.&lt;/strong&gt; Develop, test, and roll out workflows, playbooks, and tools. Simplify slow processes, verify adoption, and assign ongoing ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate operational readiness.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring together staffing, training, tooling, systems, maintenance, and support for new capabilities. Lead readiness reviews and make sure accountable owners address risks and approvals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate field needs into requirements.&lt;/strong&gt; Work alongside operators to identify constraints and partner with Engineering and other teams to deliver solutions that work in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support multiple delivery models.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify which processes can be shared and where customer or partner needs call for a different approach. Develop options and implement agreed decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communicate decisions and risks.&lt;/strong&gt; Keep teams and leaders informed about progress, changes in assumptions, and decisions needed. Document decisions, handoffs, and measures of success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in program management, operations, or a related role, with experience owning cross-functional initiatives from planning through implementation and delivering measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving day-to-day operations in a fast-paced, growing organization. You learn how work happens firsthand and connect field problems to their impact on customers and the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build integrated plans, anticipate and manage dependencies and risks, and follow through across teams. You know when to test, decide, or escalate while protecting safety and service quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use operational metrics and customer insight to diagnose root causes, weigh tradeoffs, and verify improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, including concise leadership updates and recommendations. You work through disagreements and align operators, engineers, and leaders without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical and operational systems and work effectively with subject-matter experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in engineering, logistics, business, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launching, operating, or supporting physical products or systems in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving processes across multiple sites, service models, or customer segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introducing operational tools, automation, training, or standardized workflows that teams continue to use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Else You Need to Know&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work alongside field teams where Zipline is scaling operations, solving problems on the ground and bringing what works to other sites. &lt;strong&gt;In some months, travel can account for 50–70% of your time, depending on where that work is happening.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Else You Need To Know&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting cash range for this role is $140,000 - 200,000. Please note that this is a target, starting cash range for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications for this role. The final cash pay for this role will depend on a variety of factors, including a specific candidate&#39;s experience, qualifications, skills, working location, and projected impact. The total compensation package for this role may also include: equity compensation; overtime pay; discretionary annual or performance bonuses; sales incentives; benefits such as medical, dental and vision insurance; paid time off; and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws or our own sensibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Voluntary Self-Identification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;For government reporting purposes, we ask candidates to respond to the below self-identification survey. Completion of the form is entirely voluntary. Whatever your decision, it will not be considered in the hiring process or thereafter. Any information that you do provide will be recorded and maintained in a confidential file.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;As set forth in Zipline ’s Equal Employment Opportunity policy, we do not discriminate on the basis of any protected group status under any applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
